# Deny by default: the build context is an explicit allowlist. Only what
# `go build` for ./cmd/dso and the provider plugins needs may enter the
# context. Anything not listed (local-secrets/, data/, .git/, runtime
# databases, agent state, audit scratch output, local binaries, docs) is
# excluded. Dockerfile COPY steps are explicit to match this list.
*

!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd/
!internal/
!pkg/

# Even inside the allowed directories, never ship runtime state or key
# material. Test fixtures needed by `go build` do not exist (go:embed uses
# internal/webui/assets and internal/store/sqlite/migrations only).
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-journal
**/*.rvf
**/*.rvf.lock
**/.swarm
**/.claude-flow
**/.claude
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*_test.go
**/testdata
